{
  "about": "RunSpriteRun frame group rules: which keys play which frame group. Written by RunSpriteRun; not read back.",
  "how_to_read": [
    "Rules are checked from priority 1 downwards while the player holds keys; the first rule whose keys are all held plays its group.",
    "only_if_in: when a list of group names is given, the rule only fires while the frame on screen belongs to one of those groups (for example fire plays FireLeft only while the character is in a left-facing group). null means always.",
    "Rules from frame_group_control come first. After them come the keys given to a group in Set Frame Group (source group_key): a diagonal such as W+D beats a single key, otherwise the key pressed last wins.",
    "mode loop: the group repeats while the keys are held. mode play_once: it plays through one time, will not fire again until the keys are let go, and then the next matching rule takes over.",
    "when_released says what happens when no playable key is held (or a play_once rule ends with nothing held): go to a frame (shown still), or go to a group (looping or still on its first frame). null means stay on the group's last frame.",
    "transitions: when the controls are about to play the group in to while the frame on screen is in one of the groups in from (or any group), the group in play_first plays once first, then the group in to starts. A row naming the group beats an any row. interruptible true means a change of keys stops it at once.",
    "Opposite directions (W and S, A and D) never count together, as on a joystick: the one pressed first counts until it is let go.",
    "Frame numbers are 1-based, as in RunSpriteRun. W A S D are up, left, down, right; 1 to 6 are fire buttons."
  ],
